0009:     Simulate water pixels falling under gravity into basins formed by colored obstacles.
0010: 
0011:     Input structure:
0012:     - bg = 0. Water pixels = color 1 (blue).
0013:     - Other colors form static solid structures (walls, steps, containers).
0014:     - Water starts in unstable positions above or beside basins.
0015: 
0016:     Rule:
0017:     - Each water pixel falls straight down through bg cells.
0018:     - When blocked below, it slides diagonally through the unique open side cell.
0019:     - When resting on a surface, it slides horizontally toward the nearest gap where it can fall again.
0020:     - Process repeats until no water pixel moves.
0021: 
0022:     Key insight: Water seeks the deepest reachable basin via diagonal and horizontal sliding, not just vertical fall.
0023:     """
0024:     g = np.array(grid, dtype=int).copy()
0025:     H, W = g.shape
0026:     bg = 0
0027:     water = 1
0028: 
0029:     if check_input:
