0050: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0051:     """
0052:     Recolor the large mask crop column-by-column using the separate three-row palette strip.
0053: 
0054:     Input structure:
0055:     - The background is the most common color.
0056:     - One large monochrome foreground object is the mask; its bbox is the output region and may contain background holes.
0057:     - The remaining foreground is a 3-row palette rectangle with the same width as the mask bbox: two identical color rows and one uniform row.
0058: 
0059:     Rule:
0060:     - Crop to the mask object's bbox.
0061:     - For each output column, color mask pixels with the corresponding color from the repeated palette rows.
0062:     - Replace background holes inside the crop with the palette's uniform third-row color.
